WEBVTT

00:02.470 --> 00:05.380
Cut! Okay, Okay!

00:12.090 --> 00:13.550
Good job all of you.

00:14.240 --> 00:15.800
Good Job, Suzuka-chan.

00:16.380 --> 00:17.700
Good Job.

00:21.630 --> 00:24.440
You know, I'm glad I was allowed to act.

00:25.600 --> 00:27.120
I'm not an expert...

00:27.890 --> 00:29.540
You're doing extremely well.

00:30.110 --> 00:33.730
It's hard to imagine this is your first time.

00:34.390 --> 00:38.160
You aren't quite up to my lifelike performing skill yet,

00:38.780 --> 00:42.460
But you know, you have great potential.

00:43.540 --> 00:44.660
Thank You.

00:45.410 --> 00:49.210
You wrote this story right?

00:49.930 --> 00:50.860
Is that true?

00:51.360 --> 00:55.190
About this story... I only like reading...

00:55.340 --> 01:01.060
I was worried, but onii-chan pushed me to enter the contest.

01:02.870 --> 01:05.580
Then it turned out like this...

01:07.150 --> 01:09.690
You'll do fine, don't worry.

01:09.980 --> 01:11.450
Check, please!

01:11.920 --> 01:12.830
Coming!

01:15.640 --> 01:16.880
Let's go, Suzuka-chan.

01:17.720 --> 01:18.330
Yeah.

01:36.570 --> 01:38.710
Onii-chan, I can't see anything at all.

01:39.090 --> 01:40.840
How can that be?

01:43.520 --> 01:45.390
That's weird.

01:46.670 --> 01:49.980
Is that because all the stars are gone?

01:50.070 --> 01:52.390
Time for dinner. What are you guys doing?

01:52.920 --> 01:56.010
Ah, yeah, we can't see any stars.

01:56.570 --> 01:57.850
Stars?

01:57.970 --> 02:02.420
Ah, today is the date to see the Capricorn Alpha meteor shower.

02:02.870 --> 02:05.900
Suzuka said she wants to see it.

02:06.070 --> 02:09.800
We've been looking for it, but we can't find anything at all.

02:12.360 --> 02:14.530
It's impossible to see. It's too bright here.

02:14.570 --> 02:16.480
But it's night already.

02:16.910 --> 02:20.520
If you want to observe, you won't see anything here unless it's very dark.

02:20.970 --> 02:23.610
Since city lights here are too bright...

02:23.670 --> 02:25.920
We can't really see anything even if it's midnight.

02:25.970 --> 02:29.500
Are you serious? I was really looking forward to it.

02:29.670 --> 02:31.590
A darker place? How dark would that be?

02:31.810 --> 02:33.170
Well...

02:35.970 --> 02:38.710
The place we're moving to would be good enough.

02:39.270 --> 02:40.310
Really?

02:40.670 --> 02:42.390
Yeah, for sure.

02:43.270 --> 02:46.130
That's all for today. Let's go have dinner.

02:53.070 --> 02:54.020
W-Well...

02:54.270 --> 02:57.560
What? Didn't Dad tell us we can't see anything here?

03:03.670 --> 03:05.240
I know, I know.

03:05.470 --> 03:07.760
After we move to the new house, I'll go see the stars with you.

03:08.170 --> 03:10.470
Okay, you promise?

03:11.370 --> 03:13.040
Seems like I've got no choice.

03:15.470 --> 03:21.490
Promise me now, you can't lie, can't change.

03:21.970 --> 03:23.380
Now you promised me.

03:27.070 --> 03:32.050
The Starry Sky and a Telescope

03:32.970 --> 03:35.350
The Capricorn Alpha meteor shower will be tonight...

03:35.470 --> 03:39.610
The whole nation is preparing for a Meteor Shower celebration. Everybody is very excited.

03:39.910 --> 03:41.860
However, let's look over today's weather.

03:41.920 --> 03:44.060
It's going to be really hot again.

03:44.820 --> 03:45.850
Geez.

03:47.560 --> 03:51.060
(Forget about everything you're thinking, and you will be cooled down. Prohibited use in mornings and afternoons. -by Kenji Tomosaka)

03:51.520 --> 03:55.130
Why can't I use the AC in the middle of the day?

04:03.820 --> 04:05.200
(Forget about everything you're thinking, and you will be cooled down. Prohibited use in mornings and afternoons. -by Kenji Tomosaka）

04:06.090 --> 04:14.050
Really, they're living a life ignoring the truth of the all-mighty modern science, which can even predict the appearance of meteor showers.

04:18.920 --> 04:22.470
Parasol, parasol, parasol where are you?

04:33.120 --> 04:36.300
That Kenji, putting my parasol here again.

04:59.520 --> 05:02.960
Now, take a ten minute break.

05:21.120 --> 05:22.260
Tomosaka-san.

05:24.020 --> 05:25.720
You really did a pretty good job in your club practice.

05:26.420 --> 05:28.360
Sakura-san, Tae-senpai.

05:29.020 --> 05:30.300
What's up?

05:32.820 --> 05:37.010
Hey, you'll be able to see the Capricorn Alpha meteor shower tonight, right?

05:40.020 --> 05:41.170
Meteor shower...

05:47.120 --> 05:51.750
Right? Isawa-senpai said it would be better if we all watched it together.

05:56.920 --> 05:59.030
Tomosaka-san, are you listening?

06:00.060 --> 06:05.080
Ah, yeah... Sorry, I have something to do tonight.

06:06.020 --> 06:07.080
I see.

06:09.820 --> 06:14.880
I invited Tomosaka-kun and Konoe-san just now, but they refused too.

06:15.420 --> 06:17.990
Onii-chan and Nanami-oneechan?

06:20.120 --> 06:21.430
They said they had something else to do, too.

06:21.920 --> 06:22.960
What happened?

06:28.420 --> 06:30.880
Tomosaka, practice is starting now!

06:31.920 --> 06:34.380
Sorry, I'll be right there.

06:35.020 --> 06:38.550
I still have to practice. Sorry.

06:45.820 --> 06:47.050
Please.

07:05.420 --> 07:07.090
You're not concentrating enough!

07:17.390 --> 07:18.890
Thank you for your instruction.

07:28.720 --> 07:33.150
Awesome, there're stars everywhere.

07:33.180 --> 07:36.980
That's because we couldn't see any at our old house.

07:37.320 --> 07:40.050
Ah? No stars?

07:40.620 --> 07:46.910
Dad said that's because the city lights from the houses and stores were too bright.

07:48.320 --> 07:49.750
So that's why.

07:51.920 --> 07:54.620
Since there are no malls or grocery stores...

07:54.720 --> 07:56.250
We really can see them clearly.

07:56.360 --> 07:59.050
Ah, you are laughing at the countryside again.

07:59.320 --> 08:01.730
I'm not laughing at anything.

08:02.420 --> 08:05.430
Ah, I found a new constellation!

08:06.320 --> 08:07.480
Where where?

08:08.970 --> 08:12.130
It's that star and that one, if you connect those two together.

08:12.160 --> 08:13.920
I will name it the steak curry constellation.

08:15.920 --> 08:18.030
What was that, it sounds so weird.

08:18.230 --> 08:19.620
I found another one too.

08:19.620 --> 08:20.600
Where?

08:21.720 --> 08:24.660
If you connect that star with this one here.

08:24.920 --> 08:26.610
Crab cream potato pie constellation.

08:26.620 --> 08:29.530
That's too long. Let's call it the potato pie constellation instead.

08:29.560 --> 08:33.460
No, that is the crispy crab cream potato pie constellation.

08:34.020 --> 08:35.830
Ah, I found one too.

08:36.220 --> 08:37.370
Look there.

08:38.220 --> 08:39.680
What's the name for that one?

08:39.920 --> 08:42.560
That's the tomato macaroni constellation.

08:42.690 --> 08:46.360
It's more like a meat sauce macaroni constellation to me.

08:46.620 --> 08:49.740
That's not right. It's the tomato macaroni constellation.

08:50.020 --> 08:53.030
No, it must be the meat sauce macaroni constellation.

08:54.520 --> 08:56.560
Suzuka, come here for a minute.

08:57.620 --> 08:58.490
I'm coming.

09:05.960 --> 09:08.140
Well, Onii-chan.

09:08.690 --> 09:09.550
What?

09:10.020 --> 09:12.700
Tomorrow... well...

09:13.320 --> 09:15.510
Isn't tomorrow Sunday?

09:18.720 --> 09:21.530
Well, forget it. It's nothing, really.

09:21.620 --> 09:22.900
Suzuka!

09:26.920 --> 09:28.510
What? Father?

09:33.260 --> 09:35.800
Wow, awesome!

09:35.920 --> 09:39.100
Tomorrow is the Capricorn Alpha meteor shower, right?

09:39.320 --> 09:40.930
You still remember?

09:41.520 --> 09:43.960
Don't you want to see it once together with Kenji?

09:44.190 --> 09:46.900
But I wonder if that idiot still remembers it or not.

09:47.920 --> 09:50.660
Don't worry, he must remember for sure.

09:51.820 --> 09:54.470
Thank you, I will cherish this gift.

09:58.430 --> 10:01.130
Don't tell Suzuka-chan, okay?

10:06.820 --> 10:08.520
You really have to keep this a secret, okay?

10:08.820 --> 10:12.530
I know, I won't let Suzuka know, alright?

10:12.840 --> 10:15.890
I'm so looking forward to it, tomorrow's meteor shower.

10:15.920 --> 10:17.160
Meteor shower?

10:18.820 --> 10:19.710
Suzuka?

10:19.720 --> 10:20.830
Suzuka-chan.

10:23.620 --> 10:27.080
Onii-chan, Nanami-oneechan.

10:28.920 --> 10:32.040
What is this telescope?

10:32.190 --> 10:35.760
Awesome, did Dad buy this for you?

10:35.870 --> 10:38.380
Dad really likes Suzuka.

10:45.260 --> 10:46.450
Hey, Suzuka!

10:47.370 --> 10:48.500
Suzuka-chan...

10:55.940 --> 10:57.620
Tomosaka, hurry and get up!

10:57.670 --> 10:58.300
Yes, sir!

11:30.070 --> 11:33.860
Look, look! I found this interesting thing in the garage.

11:41.170 --> 11:42.360
What's wrong?

11:44.270 --> 11:46.050
Hmm, nothing.

11:46.570 --> 11:50.370
Even though this stand is broken, we can still use it, right?

11:55.370 --> 12:00.090
I want to use this to observe the Capricorn Alpha meteor shower tonight with all of you.

12:00.770 --> 12:03.670
How about it? It's a good idea, right?

12:05.670 --> 12:08.220
I need to fix my bike tonight.

12:08.860 --> 12:10.450
Ah, Ken-chan.

12:10.670 --> 12:14.030
What was that attitude? I was really inviting you.

12:14.280 --> 12:18.170
I'll never invite you again, you motorcycle moron.

12:22.570 --> 12:26.230
Ken-chan, that... telescope...

12:26.440 --> 12:29.030
Sorry, can you leave me alone for a while, please?

12:34.270 --> 12:35.310
Ken-chan.

12:53.670 --> 12:55.760
Hikari-chan, what are you doing?

12:55.990 --> 12:58.620
This telescope isn't balanced.

12:58.970 --> 13:00.610
That telescope...

13:02.570 --> 13:05.140
What's wrong? Even you have that expression.

13:05.270 --> 13:07.420
What's wrong with all of you?

13:24.470 --> 13:27.740
You can't find that screw, right?

13:30.180 --> 13:36.230
Ken-chan, let's invite Suzuka-chan once again, okay?

13:39.070 --> 13:39.990
It's not like that.

13:42.860 --> 13:43.970
That screw...

13:54.170 --> 13:56.800
You're so loud. What the heck are you all doing up there?

13:56.840 --> 13:58.380
Dad, where is Suzuka?

13:58.670 --> 13:59.490
I don't know.

13:59.670 --> 14:01.170
Isn't she upstairs?

14:01.270 --> 14:04.380
Uncle, Nanami... Suzuka-chan is...

14:04.340 --> 14:05.950
It's not your fault.

14:09.670 --> 14:11.930
Suzuka, you are...

14:15.270 --> 14:18.840
Onii-chan, you already promised this to me...

14:23.930 --> 14:26.500
Suzuka-chan, actually, just now...

14:31.670 --> 14:36.110
I hate Onii-chan and Nanami-oneechan.

14:36.570 --> 14:37.560
Suzuka!

14:49.980 --> 14:52.580
If you're a man, you should take the responsibility.

14:59.170 --> 15:01.980
So, it was Suzuka-chan that took the screw...

15:02.860 --> 15:04.140
Yeah, maybe.

15:04.420 --> 15:05.960
If you know that, why don't you...

15:06.370 --> 15:11.210
All I could do at that time was wait for Suzuka to come back and return the screw.

15:12.570 --> 15:15.820
But I never got a chance to say that to her.

15:18.070 --> 15:19.170
Ken-chan...

15:23.490 --> 15:25.620
Suzuka-chan, Suzuka-chan.

15:26.170 --> 15:28.830
I don't want to talk with you, Nanami-oneechan.

15:30.270 --> 15:31.220
Sorry.

15:31.570 --> 15:37.790
I heard Ken-chan say that you were looking forward to tomorrow's meteor shower very much.

15:38.100 --> 15:42.870
So I wanted Mom to make some good boxed lunches to surprise you.

15:45.070 --> 15:48.860
You can go with Ken-chan tomorrow, just the two of you, okay?

15:50.070 --> 15:51.520
I will be fine.

15:52.070 --> 15:53.450
Nanami-oneechan.

16:09.070 --> 16:11.640
Hmm, I see what happened.

16:14.170 --> 16:17.280
Could it be... you're still holding on to that screw?

16:20.170 --> 16:25.100
Yeah, I see, I see, Suzuka-chan you're a lady already.

16:25.470 --> 16:27.300
N-no, it's not like that.

16:27.950 --> 16:32.730
So you're jealous of Nanami, right? So cute.

16:32.870 --> 16:35.870
I was only... the promise.

16:36.270 --> 16:38.530
Even now, I don't have any complaints about it.

16:39.270 --> 16:43.720
And I really want Onii-chan and Nanami-oneechan to live happily together.

16:44.570 --> 16:45.840
That's for sure.

16:46.370 --> 16:49.660
Being a couple with that idiot, only Nanami can do that.

16:50.070 --> 16:53.210
And they don't even realize it.

16:53.570 --> 16:56.020
That's really messed up.

17:00.770 --> 17:01.810
In that case...

17:03.770 --> 17:05.410
It should be very easy to know what we should do now.

17:09.170 --> 17:11.180
Just go ahead and apologize to them.

17:11.670 --> 17:12.270
But...

17:12.470 --> 17:15.190
Come on, how long are you going to be shy about it?

17:15.470 --> 17:18.290
Show me your judo spirit.

17:24.670 --> 17:27.110
I'll show you how to do it.

17:29.170 --> 17:30.940
Now, let me read another message.

17:31.270 --> 17:32.900
It was sent by Kitty Kitty-san.

17:33.240 --> 17:37.310
I am going to see that Capricorn Alpha meteor shower with my loved one tonight...

17:37.870 --> 17:39.870
Even though he said he will have something important to say to me.

17:39.870 --> 17:41.850
But what will he say? Could it be...?

17:42.870 --> 17:45.680
I want to request a song from when I first met him.

17:46.170 --> 17:49.820
Yeah, maybe they're promising their future to each other now.

17:50.070 --> 17:54.880
All right, here is the song you've been waiting for.
Next song, "The Meteor of Dreams"

17:57.470 --> 17:58.870
Prepare for this now...

18:00.170 --> 18:01.940
What the heck are you doing?! Wa--

18:02.310 --> 18:04.100
If you don't listen to me...

18:04.110 --> 18:07.200
Who knows what will happen to this bike...

18:07.670 --> 18:09.670
Idiot, stop!

18:10.870 --> 18:13.800
Ahh!! Please forgive me!!!

18:15.570 --> 18:17.880
Geez, what the heck do you want?

18:18.170 --> 18:19.890
All right, shut up and hurry up.

18:32.770 --> 18:36.790
Come on, go fix it. Make it balanced.

18:42.070 --> 18:43.130
Y-Yo...

18:43.770 --> 18:47.460
Onii-chan... Um.. well...

18:48.620 --> 18:51.380
Don't worry, have faith in Ken-chan.

18:53.870 --> 18:55.500
Well, I...

19:04.130 --> 19:05.080
Onii-chan.

19:21.520 --> 19:24.740
But, this telescope has been there for so long.

19:24.870 --> 19:27.330
You're still pretty good at it, man.

19:32.070 --> 19:35.110
It hurts, H-Hikari-chan.

19:35.710 --> 19:39.210
Hey, you, come with me!

19:39.470 --> 19:41.540
It hurts, hurts!

19:41.570 --> 19:47.730
Every single time Ken-chan saw that it was meteor shower season... he took out the telescope and adjusted it.

19:48.170 --> 19:49.260
Onii-chan does that?

19:49.970 --> 19:53.430
That's because he always remembers his promise with you, Suzuka-chan.

19:54.670 --> 19:55.450
Give it a try.

20:02.060 --> 20:04.990
Wow, so pretty.

20:06.970 --> 20:09.100
Sorry, I kept that promise for this long.

20:11.570 --> 20:14.280
No... Thank you, Onii-chan.

20:16.270 --> 20:18.490
Sorry, Nanami-oneechan

20:20.870 --> 20:23.450
How about it? Can you see?

20:25.770 --> 20:29.170
Awesome! Come on, everybody, take a look.

20:33.570 --> 20:34.970
It is really very beautiful.

20:50.070 --> 20:52.710
Ah, awesome.

20:59.170 --> 21:00.330
It's very pretty.

21:09.370 --> 21:11.320
That's great, Ken-chan.

21:12.160 --> 21:12.960
Yeah.

21:33.570 --> 21:36.080
Shoot, I'm going to be late for morning practice!

21:53.280 --> 21:55.180
Meteor showers are so beautiful.

21:55.180 --> 21:56.310
Yeah.

21:56.340 --> 21:58.800
Did you make your wish, Suzuka-chan?

21:58.810 --> 22:01.650
Ah, hmm, how about you, Nanami-oneechan?

22:02.280 --> 22:04.030
Ah? Well...

22:06.120 --> 22:07.780
Come on, Nanami-oneechan.

22:08.480 --> 22:09.960
You're the same though, Suzuka-chan.

22:13.080 --> 22:16.980
Next on Lamune: Three People and Two Pearls

22:16.120 --> 22:21.120
